readonly b.cue
exit 1
rerun

A write that fails partway is reported, and the module file is not
written: the module never claims a version while a file it evaluates is
still in the old form. Once the file is writable, a rerun converges: the
file already converted joins its package in the target's form and is
reported as nothing, the rest
converts, and the version is bumped.

-- cue.mod/module.cue --
module: "mod.test"

language: version: "v0.17.0"

-- a.cue --
package p

X=a: {b: X.c, c: 1}
-- b.cue --
package p

Y=b: {c: Y.d, d: 1}
-- expect/stderr --
b.cue: write: permission denied
mod upgrade: 1 file(s) could not be written; language version left at v0.17.0
-- expect/a.cue --
package p

a~(X): {b: X.c, c: 1}
-- expect2/stderr --
-- expect2/a.cue --
package p

a~(X): {b: X.c, c: 1}
-- expect2/b.cue --
package p

b~(Y): {c: Y.d, d: 1}
-- expect2/cue.mod/module.cue --
module: "mod.test"
language: version: "v0.18.0"
